  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing VDOT Implementation**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `/src/lib/vdot.ts` file, and am planning its design. My work centers on implementing the VDOT algorithm, along with the physics and math related to the running plan. A key consideration now is the formula for calculating VDOT from race/cooper, specifically the Cooper distance \'d\' covered in 12 minutes.\n\n\n**Correlating VDOT Formulas**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! The Cooper test distance can be evaluated directly using the VDOT formula. Both the VO2max calculation and the standard VDOT formula from the distance and time align, which is fantastic. The same holds true with the 2400m test. It\'s a clean correlation between the VO2max formula and VDOT, perfect! I will offer both when documenting the work.\n\n\n**Formatting Time for Output**\n\nI\'ve just written two time formatting functions to present time values. The first, `formatTime`, provides a full representation as `HhMMmSSs`. The second, `formatMMSS`, formats the time as `MM:SS`, perfect for race times and paces. I\'m focusing on providing comprehensive and readable outputs for the user. Now I\'m shifting to structuring the 8-week periodized training plan.\n\n\n**Structuring Training Phases**\n\nI\'m now deep in defining the 8-week periodized training plan, and have planned out each week. I\'ve noted the volume increases and decreases and am working to clearly articulate those changes in the descriptions, and also warning about not increasing volume and intensity together. The workout restrictions for beginners are clear. Week 7 will have a small volume decrease to facilitate high intensity work. I am focusing on the training load, now.\n\n\n**Defining Beginner Constraints**\n\nI\'ve got a critical focus on beginner programs! I\'m adding crucial workout restrictions for novice runners. They\'ll be limited to easy runs, warm-ups, and strides for the initial six weeks. Interval intensity will be set to none, or the intervals replaced with light runs. Also, I\'m now calculating and explicitly reporting the maximum interval volume, which is at most 8% of the weekly volume, so the user can see it! I\'m now implementing this functionality!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now build the core mathematics and sports science engines in `/src/lib/vdot.ts`. This library uses the real formulas from Dr. Jack Daniels\' Oxygen Power (VDOT) system and the Karvonen Heart Rate Zone formulations, rather than hardcoded mock figures. It also implements the procedural time predictor (using a high-precision binary solver for equations), and an 8-week periodized training plan generator that strictly enforces all safety rules (including the beginner restriction and the 8% limit for intervals)."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 706751379
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
