  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Organizing Components**\n\nI\'ve successfully configured the server! Now I\'m shifting focus to component creation. I\'m experimenting with organizing the components under a `/src/components/` directory. Specifically, I plan to start by building `/src/components/CoachChat.tsx`, which will implement the conversational UI for the Brazil Running Coach, handling text input and output.\n\n\n**Defining UI Components**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out the UI components! I am thinking the `/src/components/CoachChat.tsx` file will handle conversational aspects, showing suggestions, runner state context, and typing indicators. I\'m also planning a `/src/components/CalculatorTab.tsx` with interactive calculators, input fields for various runner metrics (Max HR, Volume, etc.), test estimates (Cooper, 2400m), and tables for Heart Rate Zones and Training Pace Zones. A `/src/components/Predictor` component is also in progress.\n\n\n**Expanding Feature Set**\n\nI\'m now expanding the feature set for the running coach. I\'ve conceptualized a `/src/components/Tab.tsx` component that will display estimated equivalent performances based on VDOT coefficient for various distances, with a stunning visual progress graph, or simple bento cards for equivalents, along with a disclaimer. I\'m also planning a `/src/components/PlanTab.tsx` that will visualize an 8-week periodized training plan, with weekly summaries and individual workout cards, including warnings. Finally, `/src/components/RecoveryTab.tsx` is being designed, incorporating an interactive overtraining risk assessment quiz and displaying risk levels with an explicit medical warning for sharp pain.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/components/CalculatorTab.tsx`. This file contains the complete interactive calculator suite: Max and Resting HR configuration, direct VDOT entry, plus interactive test processors for the Cooper (12m) and 2400m physical assessments. It outputs heart rate zones computed using the Karvonen formula and training paces calculated from Jack Daniels\' VDOT formulas. It dynamically shows warnings for beginners (if high intensity is set too early) and highlights the volume/intensity limit guideline."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 998364965
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
