    thinking: "**Designing the RecoveryTab**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `RecoveryTab.tsx` component. The focus is on creating interactive elements for overtraining considerations. I\'m aiming for a responsive design with dynamic validations, just like `PlanTab.tsx`, ensuring 100% adherence to safety constraints. This tab should be as equally beautiful as the `PlanTab.tsx`!\n\n\n**Assessing the Checklist**\n\nI\'ve just added an exhaustion checklist with five key questions focused on fatigue, mood, heart rate, sleep, and pain. I\'m building in a risk score evaluation system based on the responses: Normal, Moderate, or Severe risk levels will be calculated based on the number of \'yes\' answers, and I\'ve also implemented a \'Severe Pain Guard\' that presents a prominent warning, in red, with a doctor\'s checkmark, whenever the acute pain question is selected.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/components/RecoveryTab.tsx` to handle the \"Recomendar Descanso e Preven\303\247\303\243o\" actions (COMANDO 5). It contains an interactive overtraining assessment. It features dynamic state evaluation for fatigue and includes a physical health guard: if the user selects localized sharp pain (such as in the knees, shins, or tendons), it immediately displays custom warnings instructing them to suspend training and seek professional medical guidance. It also details standard protocols for active recovery."
