  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Inspecting CalculatorTab.tsx**\n\nI\'m focusing now on `CalculatorTab.tsx`. My current thought is to inspect the file content, specifically `/src/components/CalculatorTab.tsx`, to identify elements suitable for high-contrast dark classes and modern styled components before making any changes to the file. This analysis is the next step to refactor the file.\n\n\n**Analyzing Dark Theme Adaptations**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing specific components within `CalculatorTab.tsx` for dark theme adaptation. For instance, I\'ve identified the \"card-configs-running\" div and thought about modifying its background, border, and shadow. I plan to change the title icon and text color for better contrast, and adjust the level selector label and styling. I can then modify custom styles and properties for the select and input elements.\n\n\n**Reviewing Global Styles**\n\nI\'m now reviewing the existing global styles, specifically the `index.css` file. I\'ve realized that the global CSS rules already handle the dark background, white text, and border for input and select elements, preventing the need for individual styling. This simplifies adapting the direct VDOT override inputs, as I just need to focus on adding paddings, font styles, and containers.\n\n\n**Modifying Direct VDOT Input**\n\nI am now focusing on the direct VDOT input elements and applying the dark theme adaptations. I am considering the button\'s class name, particularly the \"Aplicar\" button. I\'ve decided to change the existing classes, focusing on the background color, text color, and hover effect. The objective is to enhance the visual contrast and modern feel, aiming for a consistent style across the component. I\'m swapping the `bg-indigo-600` for `bg-[#FF4E00]`.\n\n\n**Evaluating Safety Guideline Box**\n\nI\'m now evaluating the safety guidelines box, particularly the `id=\"safety-guidelines-box\"` in `CalculatorTab.tsx`. The default amber tones are a consideration, but I\'m thinking black text on neon orange might offer beautiful, perfect contrast. I need to ensure it works nicely.\n\n\n**Refining Styling Enhancements**\n\nI\'ve been improving the safety guideline box; the dark theme styling is now deeply amber on translucent black with amber borders, significantly improving contrast and aesthetics. I\'m focusing on text contrast within the box, optimizing for dark themes. I have also moved on to the next element: `testing-methods-card`.\n\n\n**Updating Testing Methods**\n\nI\'ve just revised the \"testing-methods-card\" element, updating its styling. I changed the background to a darker tone (`#0A0A0A`) with rounded corners, a white border, and a shadow for a modern look. The text\'s color is white, with a bold, uppercase title. I then refactored the Cooper/2400m test elements, altering the background from `bg-gray-50/40` to `bg-white/5` for a refined appearance.\n\n\n**Refactoring Button Styles**\n\nI\'m now refactoring button styles to improve visual contrast and aesthetics, particularly focusing on the \"Aplicar\" button. I\'m updating the class names. I\'m changing the background to `#FF4E00`, the text to black, the font to extra bold, and I am adding a subtle hover effect and adjusting the text color. The goal is to enhance the modern feel.\n\n\n**Styling VO2Max Results**\n\nI\'ve just styled the VO2Max results section. I updated the background to `bg-white/5`, added a white border, rounded corners, and padding. I then switched the title\'s color to `#FF4E00` for excellent contrast, and used a white font for VO2Max and VDOT values. I also have the italic note at the bottom. The dark theme styling is now perfect! I\'m now turning my attention to the Pace and HR cards, and their dark-theme styling.\n\n\n"
