  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have successfully resolved the transient Gemini API issues and improved overall application stability. Here is a summary of the optimizations:\n\n- **Enhanced Resiliency with Fallback Chains**: Configured `generateContentWithRetry` in `server.ts` to implement a multi-model fallback routine. If the primary model (`gemini-3.5-flash`) faces temporary spikes in demand or unavailability (HTTP 503), the server now automatically falls back and retries using the lightweight and high-availability model `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`.\n- **Exponential Backoff**: Integrated randomized scale multipliers during transient retries to avoid rate limits and back-pressure issues under high demand.\n- **Client Processing Guards**: Wrapped response parsing blocks inside the React components with safety guards to guarantee the chat interface gracefully and non-disruptively displays fallback messages even during external downtime events."
