  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Tab Structure**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing a RacesTab component. It seems straightforward, beginning with the necessary state variables. I\'ll need to figure out what data the tab needs to present effectively, with a design that is elegant and maintainable. I need to be sure the application is scalable.\n\n\n**Defining Race Data**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of race data. I want to build a rich dataset for Brazilian running races. I\'m considering attributes like name, location, date, distances, website URLs, elevation profiles (with a descriptive metric), and a course difficulty factor for VDOT adjustments. I\'m also including key highlights for each race. I\'ve begun with the \"Maratona do Rio\" as a starting point.\n\n\n**Expanding Race Data**\n\nI\'ve fleshed out some more race details. I\'ve added specifics for the \"SP City Marathon\" and \"Maratona de Porto Alegre,\" including dates, profiles, elevation gains, and difficulty factors. I\'m noting key highlights and also URLs for reference. The goal is a dataset that\'s both informative and useful.\n\n\n**Adding Race Data Points**\n\nI\'ve just added three more races to the dataset. These include the \"Corrida Internacional de S\303\243o Silvestre\" with its challenging profile and historical significance, the \"Meia Maratona Internacional do Rio\" known for its fast course, and the \"Volta Internacional da Pampulha\" with its scenic route. I\'ve noted dates, distances, profiles, gains, and difficulty factors for each. Each also has a unique detail and link.\n\n\n**Incorporating More Races**\n\nI\'ve just added the \"Maratona de Curitiba,\" \"Meia Maratona de Bras\303\255lia,\" and \"Maratona Internacional de Florian\303\263polis\" to the dataset. I focused on dates, distances, profiles, gains, and a difficulty factor for VDOT adjustments for each. I\'m taking care to include those crucial details, highlights, and links to the relevant websites.\n\n\n**Implementing Dynamic Search**\n\nI\'m now grappling with implementing a dynamic search function. The goal is a smart search field that accepts custom race names or cities. I am considering several strategies. I\'m exploring a built-in search or generator simulation to instantly process the input. The aim is to create a customized, themed race profile card that integrates well with the VDOT theme.\n\n\n**Enhancing User Engagement**\n\nI\'ve made significant strides in making the interface more engaging! I am now working on a new calculator to interactively adjust race predictions with custom elevation. The result is a truly responsive search with a VDOT-themed race profile card that integrates well! I am thrilled to design `/src/components/RacesTab.tsx` with safe imports and interactive components like the prediction calculator.\n\n\n**Simulating Race Profiles**\n\nI\'m now implementing the simulated Google Search Engine functionality. The search bar is now live with the prompt \"\360\237\224\215 N\303\243o encontrou sua prova? Digite o nome da cidade ou corrida aqui...\" I am excited to generate race profiles that match user queries in real-time. I will assign elevations, websites, and VDOT ratings. I have pre-programmed races to support realistic queries too: \"Meia de Pomerode\" will be coded with a +60m elevation gain and a +0.2 difficulty factor. A \"Buenos Aires\" race is defined as \"Super plano\".\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create a brand new file `/src/components/RacesTab.tsx` to build the requested \"Corridas no Brasil\" feature. This interactive dashboard will compile real, prestigious Brazilian races, calculate specific target times adapted to each course\'s elevation profile and environmental factors, and simulate a Google search style finder to dynamically generate custom profiles and advice for any race entered!"
