  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Goal**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the objective, which is to provide the expert, ScrapingArchitect, with help. I\'m focusing on clarifying how this help should be delivered and what specific actions are needed. I\'m also ensuring the persona (ScrapingArchitect) is maintained as a senior software engineer.\n\n\n**Outlining the Architecture**\n\nI\'ve decided on an architecture for automatically monitoring Brazilian street running events. I\'ll use the Bing Web Search API, supplementing it with data from structured registries like Ticket Sports. I\'m building a high-level plan and architectural overview, covering database design, serverless functions on Vercel, and potential cron setups. I\'m focusing on a polished, technical delivery to the user, like a direct, actionable solution.\n\n\n**Clarifying User Intent**\n\nI\'m now wrestling with the implied request. Initially, I was unsure if the user wanted a stand-alone Vite app or architectural guidance for an existing project. Analyzing the instructions, I see that I\'m meant to adopt the \"ScrapingArchitect\" persona and deliver a comprehensive architectural guide, including the serverless function, Supabase database, and Bing Web Search API integration. This aims for a complete, actionable solution.\n\n\n**Evaluating Implementation Options**\n\nI\'m now weighing the best approach to present this. I\'m considering adding an interactive dashboard directly to our current application versus delivering a top-notch engineering response that outlines everything. The key is helping the user build the app on Vercel to avoid costs. I\'m leaning toward a detailed architectural breakdown including SQL schema, Vercel Serverless Function code (TypeScript), and a Cron setup. I want to balance clarity with an elegant presentation.\n\n\n**Crafting the Response**\n\nI\'ve decided to craft the response directly in Portuguese, maintaining the ScrapingArchitect persona. I\'m focusing on providing a clean SQL schema for Supabase, specifically for the `corridas_detectadas` table. This includes fields for event details, city, state, distances, links, and source. I\'m prioritizing data integrity and efficient storage.\n\n\n**Refining the SQL Schema**\n\nI\'m now honing the SQL schema, paying particular attention to data integrity and access control. I\'ve defined the `updated_at` and `created_at` fields with the UTC timezone, as well as a default policy for public read access. I\'ve also implemented a restrictive policy, ensuring write/update operations on the `corridas_detectadas` table are exclusively controlled by the service role.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Sauda\303\247\303\265es. Aqui fala o **ScrapingArchitect**. \n\nExcelente escolha t\303\251cnica e \303\251tica. Ao optar pela **Op\303\247\303\243o 1 (Bing Web Search API)** em sinergia com o mapeamento e parsing direcionado de grandes agregadores de inscri\303\247\303\265es (como *Ticket Sports*, *Sympla*, *Corre Brasil* e *Federa\303\247\303\265es Estaduais*), criamos uma arquitetura robusta, legalmente em conformidade, imune a CAPTCHAs agressivos e perfeitamente otimizada para o ecossistema Serverless da Vercel.\n\nAbaixo, apresento o projeto completo de engenharia para ligar o **Crawler Serverless (Vercel Node.js)** ao **Banco de Dados Cloud (Supabase)** utilizando a API do Bing e t\303\251cnicas seguras de parsing.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\217\233\357\270\217 Arquitetura Geral do Sistema\n\n```\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202    Vercel Cron Job      \342\224\202 (Disparador Di\303\241rio)\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n             \342\224\202 (HTTP POST /api/cron-crawl)\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\274\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202 Vercel Serverless Func  \342\224\202 (Node.js runtime - processamento intercalado por blocos)\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n       \342\224\202            \342\224\202\n       \342\224\202 (GET)      \342\224\202 (GET / Fetch de p\303\241ginas estruturadas)\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\274\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220   \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\226\274\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202  Bing API   \342\224\202   \342\224\202 Ticket Sports /    \342\224\202 (Heur\303\255sticas & seletores r\303\241pidos)\n\342\224\202  (JSON)     \342\224\202   \342\224\202 Corre Brasil / etc \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n       \342\224\202            \342\224\202\n       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n             \342\224\202 (Upsert - Resolu\303\247\303\243o de Duplicados por Link)\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\274\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202    Supabase DB Cloud    \342\224\202 (Tabela `corridas_detectadas` com RLS habilitado)\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n```\n\n---\n\n### 1. Modelagem do Banco de Dados (Supabase SQL)\n\nPara garantir integridade de dados e facilidade de leitura pelo front-end, utilizaremos o seguinte esquema SQL. O ponto crucial de resili\303\252ncia aqui \303\251 a restri\303\247\303\243o `unique` na coluna `link`, permitindo o uso de opera\303\247\303\265es de `upsert` (evitando duplica\303\247\303\265es de registros ao rodar o crawler m\303\272ltiplas vezes).\n\nExecute este bloco de comando no **SQL Editor** do seu Supabase Dashboard:\n\n```sql\n-- Habilitar extens\303\243o para gera\303\247\303\243o de UUIDs, se n\303\243o estiver ativa\ncreate extension if not exists \"uuid-ossp\";\n\n-- Criar a tabela de corridas de rua unificada\ncreate table public.corridas_detectadas (\n    id uuid default uuid_generate_v4() primary key,\n    titulo text not null,\n    data_evento date,\n    data_texto text, -- Armazena strings como \"Setembro, 2026\" caso a data exata falhe no parse\n    cidade text not null,\n    estado varchar(2) not null,\n    local_completo text,\n    distancias jsonb default \'[]\'::jsonb, -- Ex: [\"5k\", \"10k\", \"21k\"]\n    link text unique not null, -- Previne duplicidade baseado no link da inscri\303\247\303\243o\n    fonte text not null, -- Ex: \"Bing Search\", \"Ticket Sports\", \"Sympla\"\n    perfil_terreno varchar(20) default \'moderate\', -- \'flat\', \'hilly\', \'extreme\', \'moderate\'\n    created_at timestamp with time zone default timezone(\'utc\'::text, now()) not null,\n    updated_at timestamp with time zone default timezone(\'utc\'::text, now()) not null\n);\n\n-- Habilitar Row Level Security (RLS)\nalter table public.corridas_detectadas enable row level security;\n\n-- Pol\303\255tica 1: Permitir leitura livre p\303\272blica (\303\272til para exibir na aplica\303\247\303\243o)\ncreate policy \"Leitura p\303\272blica para qualquer usu\303\241rio\" \n    on public.corridas_detectadas \n    for select \n    using (true);\n\n-- Pol\303\255tica 2: Permitir escrita (insert/update/delete) apenas usando a chave secreta de servi\303\247o (Service Role)\ncreate policy \"Escrita restrita ao crawler\" \n    on public.corridas_detectadas \n    for all \n    using (auth.role() = \'service_role\');\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. O Crawler Serverless (Vercel Function em TypeScript)\n\nA Vercel limita as rotas serverless do plano gratuito a **10 segundos** de execu\303\247\303\243o por requisi\303\247\303\243o (ou **60 segundos** no plano Pro). Motores como Puppeteer consomem muita CPU e facilmente estourariam esse limite na Vercel. \n\nUtilizando a API do Bing e um parser de dados via express\303\265es regulares estruturadas, realizamos o processamento em **milissegundos**.\n\nCrie este arquivo na raiz da sua aplica\303\247\303\243o Vercel sob `/api/cron-crawl.ts` (ou `/api/cron-crawl.js` adaptando a tipagem):\n\n```typescript\nimport { createClient } from \'@supabase/supabase-js\';\nimport type { VercelRequest, VercelResponse } from \'@vercel/node\';\n\n// Inicializa\303\247\303\243o do cliente Supabase usando vari\303\241veis de ambiente seguras\nconst supabaseUrl = process.env.SUPABASE_URL || \'\';\nconst supabaseServiceKey = process.env.SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY || \'\'; // Chave de servi\303\247o para burlar o bloqueio de escrita do RLS\nconst bingApiKey = process.env.BING_SEARCH_API_KEY || \'\';\n\nconst supabase = createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseServiceKey);\n\ninterface BingWebResult {\n  name: string;\n  url: string;\n  snippet: string;\n}\n\nexport default async function handler(req: VercelRequest, res: VercelResponse) {\n  // Garantir que a chamada \303\251 autorizada pelo Cron da Vercel ou por token secreto personalizado\n  const authHeader = req.headers.authorization;\n  if (authHeader !== `Bearer ${process.env.CRON_SECRET}`) {\n    return res.status(401).json({ error: \'N\303\243o autorizado.\' });\n  }\n\n  try {\n    // Escolhe dinamicamente um estado brasileiro a cada execu\303\247\303\243o di\303\241ria para n\303\243o extrapolar limites da Vercel\n    const estados = [\'AL\', \'PE\', \'BA\', \'CE\', \'SP\', \'RJ\', \'MG\', \'RS\', \'SC\', \'PR\', \'DF\', \'AM\', \'GO\'];\n    const diaDoAno = new Date().getDate();\n    const estadoAlvo = estados[diaDoAno % estados.length];\n\n    // Montar query otimizada focando em portais de inscri\303\247\303\243o consolidados\n    const searchQuery = `site:ticketsports.com.br/e/ OR site:sympla.com.br \"corrida\" \"2026\" \"${estadoAlvo}\"`;\n    const bingUrl = `https://api.bing.microsoft.com/v7.0/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(searchQuery)}&count=15&mkt=pt-BR`;\n\n    const bingResponse = await fetch(bingUrl, {\n      headers: { \'Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key\': bingApiKey },\n    });\n\n    if (!bingResponse.ok) {\n      throw new Error(`Falha ao invocar API do Bing: ${bingResponse.statusText}`);\n    }\n\n    const data = await bingResponse.json();\n    const results: BingWebResult[] = data.webPages?.value || [];\n\n    const corridasParaInserir = [];\n\n    for (const item of results) {\n      // Extrair informa\303\247\303\265es estruturadas a partir das strings de Snippet e URL\n      const extraidos = extrairMetadados(item.name, item.snippet, item.url, estadoAlvo);\n      if (extraidos) {\n        corridasParaInserir.push(extraidos);\n      }\n    }\n\n    if (corridasParaInserir.length === 0) {\n      return res.status(200).json({ message: `Scraping completo para o estado ${estadoAlvo}. Nenhuma nova corrida estruturada foi detectada.` });\n    }\n\n    // Upsert no Supabase usando o link \303\272nico do evento como restri\303\247\303\243o\n    const { data: dbData, error: dbError } = await supabase\n      .from(\'corridas_detectadas\')\n      .upsert(corridasParaInserir, { onConflict: \'link\' });\n\n    if (dbError) throw dbError;\n\n    return res.status(200).json({\n      status: \'Sucesso\',\n      estadoProcessado: estadoAlvo,\n      totalResultadosBing: results.length,\n      inseridosOuAtualizados: corridasParaInserir.length\n    });\n\n  } catch (error: any) {\n    return res.status(500).json({ error: error.message });\n  }\n}\n\n// Mecanismo de Intelig\303\252ncia do Crawler para traduzir strings em registros estruturados\nfunction extrairMetadados(tituloOriginal: string, snippet: string, url: string, estado: string) {\n  // Limpar formata\303\247\303\265es t\303\255picas do Bing\n  const titulo = tituloOriginal.replace(/ - Ticket Sports.*$/i, \'\').replace(/ \\| Sympla.*$/i, \'\').trim();\n\n  // Dedu\303\247\303\243o de Cidade usando Express\303\265es Regulares no snippet\n  let cidade = \"Capital\";\n  const regexCidade = /(?:em|na cidade de|no|localizado em|percurso em)\\s+([A-Z][a-z\303\240-\303\272]+(?:\\s+[A-Z][a-z\303\240-\303\272]+)*)/;\n  const matchCidade = snippet.match(regexCidade);\n  if (matchCidade && matchCidade[1]) {\n    cidade = matchCidade[1].trim();\n  }\n\n  // Dedu\303\247\303\243o de Dist\303\242ncias comuns\n  const distancias: string[] = [];\n  if (/5\\s*k/i.test(snippet + titulo)) distancias.push(\"5k\");\n  if (/10\\s*k/i.test(snippet + titulo)) distancias.push(\"10k\");\n  if (/21\\s*k|meia\\s*maratona/i.test(snippet + titulo)) distancias.push(\"Meia Maratona (21.1k)\");\n  if (/42\\s*k|maratona/i.test(snippet + titulo)) distancias.push(\"Maratona (42.2k)\");\n  if (distancias.length === 0) distancias.push(\"5k\", \"10k\"); // Padr\303\243o\n\n  // Dedu\303\247\303\243o de Data\n  let dataTexto = \"Data a confirmar\";\n  let dataEvento: string | null = null;\n  const regexData = /(\\d{2})\\/(\\d{2})\\/(2026|2027)/;\n  const matchData = snippet.match(regexData);\n  if (matchData) {\n    dataEvento = `${matchData[3]}-${matchData[2]}-${matchData[1]}`;\n    dataTexto = `${matchData[1]}/${matchData[2]}/${matchData[3]}`;\n  } else {\n    // Busca textual ex: \"20 de setembro\"\n    const regexDataTexto = /(\\d{1,2}\\s+de\\s+[a-z]+(?:\\s+de\\s+2026)?)/i;\n    const matchDataTexto = (snippet + titulo).match(regexDataTexto);\n    if (matchDataTexto) {\n      dataTexto = matchDataTexto[1] + \", 2026\";\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Define fonte baseado no dom\303\255nio do link\n  const fonte = url.includes(\'ticketsports.com.br\') ? \'Ticket Sports\' : \'Sympla\';\n\n  // Filtro preventivo de falso positivo\n  if (!titulo || titulo.length < 5) return null;\n\n  return {\n    titulo,\n    data_evento: dataEvento,\n    data_texto: dataTexto,\n    cidade,\n    estado,\n    distancias,\n    link: url,\n    fonte,\n    perfil_terreno: \'moderate\' // Classifica\303\247\303\243o inicial padr\303\243o\n  };\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Configurando o Cron Job Efetivo (`vercel.json`)\n\nPara que a fun\303\247\303\243o acima rode sem que voc\303\252 precise acionar nenhum bot\303\243o ou manter computadores ligados, configure o agendador padr\303\243o da Vercel.\n\nCrie ou edite o arquivo `vercel.json` na raiz do seu projeto:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"crons\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"/api/cron-crawl\",\n      \"schedule\": \"0 4 * * *\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n*Este cron agenda o rob\303\264 para rodar pontualmente todos os dias \303\240s 04:00 AM UTC (garantindo descoberta cont\303\255nua sem consumir toda a sua cota di\303\241ria de Bing API).*\n\n---\n\n### 4. Vari\303\241veis de Ambiente Necess\303\241rias (Production Setup)\n\nConfigure estas chaves na aba **Settings > Environment Variables** do seu painel corporativo da Vercel:\n\n1. `SUPABASE_URL`: A URL do seu projeto Supabase (Ex: `https://yourdomain.supabase.co`).\n2. `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`: A chave secreta denominada `service_role` (encontrada em *Settings > API* no Supabase). Ela \303\251 necess\303\241ria para ignorar barreiras de seguran\303\247a do RLS e persistir os registros.\n3. `BING_SEARCH_API_KEY`: Sua chave obtida no painel gratuito do Microsoft Azure Cognitive Services.\n4. `CRON_SECRET`: Um Token rand\303\264mico e imprevis\303\255vel que voc\303\252 mesmo cria (ex: `super_hash_123_456`) para evitar que invasores externos forcem requisi\303\247\303\265es cobradas na sua API de forma manual.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\222\241 Recomenda\303\247\303\265es e Boas Pr\303\241ticas do ScrapingArchitect\n\n* **Respeito aos Crawl-Delay e Portais de Origem**: Utilizar a API de pesquisa (Bing) evita que precisemos fazer milhares de conex\303\265es de raw scraping nos portais de origem. N\303\263s deixamos a infraestrutura do Bing fazer a indexa\303\247\303\243o pesada e n\303\263s apenas colhemos os frutos formatados de forma inteligente.\n* **Gargalos de Escala**: Rodar por estados selecionados alternando a cada dia (como implementado no c\303\263digo) garante que voc\303\252 fique permanentemente dentro do limite de requisi\303\247\303\265es gratuitas sem gastar fundos.\n* **Consumo de UI**: Para renderizar na aplica\303\247\303\243o, basta usar o SDK nativo `@supabase/supabase-js` em modo p\303\272blico direto no seu React Tab (`select * from corridas_detectadas`). Como nosso RLS p\303\272blico \303\251 `true` nas leituras, as listagens aparecer\303\243o instantaneamente para o seu atleta de forma din\303\242mica!"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 961034492
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
