  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying Intentions**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got it. I\'m focusing on whether the user seeks a ready-made solution for Firebase/auth/Cloud SQL, or if they are asking for guidance on a system design and an implementation framework. A quick re-read of the prompt clarified the direction.\n\n\n**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the architectural plan. The objective is clear: explain how to build a system for gathering race registration data. I\'ll outline the risk of directly scraping search results, especially Google, and then highlight the strengths of using the Bing Web Search API, complemented by scraping structured portals, like Ticket Sports and Corre Brasil. The prompt also implies an option for custom, local scraping, which I\'ll mention.\n\n\n**Developing API Architecture**\n\nI am currently fleshing out the API architecture on Vercel with Supabase, specifically the database tables with a SQL schema and cron job configuration. I\'m focusing on a secure, serverless Node.js typescript scraper setup. I\'m excited about creating a real API route like `/api/scrape-races` to simulate Bing Search/web scraping for users within the Coach Chat or `RacesTab`. I\'m planning a control panel in the UI to trigger scrapes, visualize extracted data, and simulate Supabase insertion. It\342\200\231s essential to gracefully handle secret variables, such as the Bing Web Search API key.\n\n\n**Implementing Fallbacks**\n\nI\'m now integrating robust fallback mechanisms for missing API keys. Specifically, if `process.env.BING_API_KEY` or `process.env.SUPABASE_URL` are absent, I\'ll simulate a scrape using mock data, while warning the user to configure `.env.example`. This builds a full, functioning capability. The API endpoint `/api/scrape-races` will handle the logic: query with the Bing API if keys are present; else, gracefully degrade to mocks.\n\n\n**Exploring Gemini Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating Gemini API as a sophisticated fallback. It will simulate scraping Bing search results when the Bing API key is missing, providing realistic race data extraction. The integration will use Gemini as a simulated \"scraper engine,\" emulating extraction from structured portals like Ticket Sports, Corre Brasil, and others for race name, date, and location. This allows full functionality even without external API keys. I also added Supabase and Vercel Cron instructions.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view the `.env.example` file to verify what environment variables are currently documented for the user."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 475319934
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
